            <div class="cs-heading-body-group">
              <h2 class="cs-heading">What I recommended they do next</h2>
              <p class="cs-body">
                Since the client owned the analytics and I did not have access
                to post launch data, so I could not tell them whether any of
                this worked. But I told them what to measure: how long it takes
                from when someone first opens the app until they get my first
                suggestion, and also how long it takes to complete each part of
                the on-boarding and the assessment. I wanted to know where
                people are leaving the process, is it at a specific screen, or
                somewhere in the middle of the overall flow? And then there's
                the conversion rate at the screen where you choose a new plan,
                because essentially, this is the main part of the project.
              </p>
              <p class="cs-body">
                I mentioned this at the time, not after the fact. We should also
                conduct user testing on the new on-boarding process with people
                who aren't connected to each other.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="cs-outcomes-grid">
              {
                OUTCOMES.map((o) => (
                  <div class="cs-outcome-card">
                    <>
                      <h4>{o.title}</h4>
                      <p>{o.body}</p>
                    </>
                  </div>
                ))
              }
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section id="asx-reflection" class="cs-section cs-section--reflection">
        <div class="cs-section__inner">
          <div class="cs-section__number">13<span>Reflection</span></div>
          <div>
            <div class="cs-body-group">
              <p class="cs-body">
                This redesign wasn’t about adding any new features. Most of the
                platform's best features were already there. It was about making
                it easier for users to discover those features, understand them,
                and make it easier to use them. This particular project came the
                closest to my wish of doing a consumer UX project. Even then I
                couldn’t conduct the study due to the time bound nature of the
                project, user data access and the fact that the analytics were
                sitting on the client's end. Still, I did whatever I could based
                on the constraint and made sure which part of my report was an
                evidence and which one was subjective judgment.
              </p>

              <p class="cs-body">
                What I would have changed about the project was its closure. I
                proposed a measurement plan but was unable to see any numbers.
                Whether bringing up the payments feature earlier in the
                onboarding process was good or bad, I cannot be sure yet. This
                left me incomplete and frustrated. In the future I will make
                sure that there is a provision to access the post-launch
                data. In my next project, I want something that will give me the
                chance to actually use the UX methods I've learned.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <CaseStudyFooter
        title="Let's build something together"
        sub="Have questions about this case study or looking to collaborate on consumer AI products, activation funnels and mobile personalization?"
      />
